%\subsection{Time lags}


  ## Population cycles -- Time lags
  {\bf Logistic growth with time lag}
  \[]
  where \\
  
    * $r_{max}$ is the growth rate when $N_t$ is close to 0. \\
    * $K$ is the carrying capacity
    * $lag$ is an integer (0,1,2,\dots) used to reference earlier
      time point
  




[]
  ## Time lags
```{r, Nl5,include=FALSE,echo=FALSE,fig.width=8,fig.height=6}
Nl5 <- Nl
Nl5[] <- 2
Nl5[] <- 3
Nl5[] <- 4
for(t in 4:T) {
    Nl5[] <- Nl5[] + Nl5[]*1.1*(1-Nl5[]/K)
}
plot(Nl5, type="l", xlab="Time (t)", ylab="Population size (N)",
     cex.lab=1.3, panel.first=abline(h=K, col="blue", lty=2),
     col="darkslategray3",
     lwd=4, main="r=1.1, K=50, lag=2")
@
<center>
  ![](figure/Nl5-1)
</center>



%\subsection{Cyclic carrying capacity}



  ## Population cycles -- cyclic carrying capacity
  {\bf Carrying capacity changes every year}
  \begin{gather*}
    K_t = k_0 + k_1\cos\left(\frac{2 \pi t}{c}\right) \\
    \uncover<2>{N_{t+1} = N_t + N_t r_{max}\left(1 - \frac{N_t}{K_t}\right)}
  \end{gather*}






